import Mathlib

namespace Erdos550

/-
# Erdős Problem 550

Let $m_1 \leq \cdots \leq m_k$ and $n$ be sufficiently large. If $T$ is a tree on $n$
vertices and $G$ is the complete multipartite graph with vertex class sizes
$m_1, \ldots, m_k$, then
$$R(T, G) \leq (\chi(G) - 1)(R(T, K_{m_1, m_2}) - 1) + m_1.$$

Proved by Eric Li, combining an off-Turán tree-embedding theorem with a compactness-and-
rounding theorem for represented bounded-rank hypergraph obstructions; the embedding
theorem follows from Szemerédi regularity and a local regular-matching embedding lemma of
Hladký and Piguet.

Since $G$ is complete multipartite with $k$ classes, $\chi(G) = k$, which is why the bound
below carries the factor `k - 1`. `ramsey J L` is the two-colour Ramsey number
`sInf {N | ∀ G : SimpleGraph (Fin N), J ⊑ G ∨ L ⊑ Gᶜ}` using Mathlib's `IsContained`, and
`Kmult`/`Kbip` are Mathlib's `completeMultipartiteGraph`/`completeBipartiteGraph`.

The 133 modules in the closure of `erdos_550` are flattened here in dependency order. The
upstream comparator harness is outside that closure and is not included. Note that
erdosproblems.com still lists this problem as open, pending human review of the
accompanying manuscript; what is recorded here is the machine-checked Lean development.

Nine proof sites differ from upstream. `grind` treats theorems of the current module as
E-matching candidates, so collapsing 133 modules into one file puts every project lemma
into its search space; thirteen `grind` calls that succeed module-by-module fail here.
Each was replaced by an explicit proof, or given the lemma it needed (`grind [...]`), using
only lemmas the development already proves -- `pred_unique`, `seedDeleted_adj_iff`,
`shrubF_card_eq_resAux`, `shrubF_rank_le`, `mem_componentSeeds_iff`,
`seedComponent_eq_of_seedDeleted_adj`. No statement was weakened and no new result added.
-/

